{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00729",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.44,
      "end_seconds": 16.04,
      "duration_seconds": 13.6,
      "text": "Er, hi. I've got a lump on my neck, at the back, and it's gone sore. It's a cyst, I think. I've had them before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.81,
      "end_seconds": 24.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Let me hear about it. How long has it been there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.07,
      "end_seconds": 37.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "Ages. A year? It was small and didn't bother me. Then last week it got big and sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.15,
      "end_seconds": 42.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Painful how?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.22,
      "end_seconds": 50.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Tender. Throbs a bit. It hurts if my collar rubs it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.36,
      "end_seconds": 58.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Any discharge, or has it burst?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.47,
      "end_seconds": 64.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "No. Nothing came out. No."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.5,
      "end_seconds": 71.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "What are you using on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.36,
      "end_seconds": 86.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.22,
      "text": "Doxycycline, 100 mg, the dentist gave me some, maybe once a day? And the antiseptic wash, I don't know the name, from the pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.25,
      "end_seconds": 101.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "Thanks. So doxycycline, 100 mg, once a day as you recall it. And the wash, you can't name it. Have you had cysts before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.78,
      "end_seconds": 109.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "One on my back, they cut it out, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.78,
      "end_seconds": 116.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Does it run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.71,
      "end_seconds": 122.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "My dad gets them. On his scalp."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.65,
      "end_seconds": 129.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Let me look. Which side? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.65,
      "end_seconds": 151.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Back of the neck, a bit to the right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.77,
      "end_seconds": 166.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.02,
      "text": "It's a round, firm lump about two centimetres across, tender, with a tiny dark dot in the middle. The skin around is slightly red. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.32,
      "end_seconds": 172.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Is that a cyst, then? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.62,
      "end_seconds": 187.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.43,
      "text": "It looks like an epidermoid cyst, which is a sac under the skin, and it's a little inflamed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.74,
      "end_seconds": 192.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Will it go away? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.6,
      "end_seconds": 211.2,
      "duration_seconds": 15.6,
      "text": "Inflamed ones often settle for a while, but the sac stays, and it usually flares again. Taking the whole sac out is the proper cure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.71,
      "end_seconds": 215.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Operation? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.29,
      "end_seconds": 230.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "A small one, under local anaesthetic. First, I'd like to arrange an ultrasound, to check the size and make sure it's what I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.31,
      "end_seconds": 235.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.55,
      "end_seconds": 250.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "Keep the area clean, don't squeeze it, and put a warm flannel on it for ten minutes a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.21,
      "end_seconds": 259.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Squeeze is what I want to do. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.08,
      "end_seconds": 269.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "I know, but squeezing pushes the contents deeper and can cause an infection. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.37,
      "end_seconds": 272.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.09,
      "end_seconds": 289.36,
      "duration_seconds": 13.27,
      "text": "If it turns very red and hot, gets much more painful, starts to ooze pus, or you get a fever, come back that day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.58,
      "end_seconds": 294.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "I will. Thanks. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.54,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "And if the ultrasound confirms it, we'll talk about getting it removed once it's calm. ~"
    }
  ]
}
